findings.body:
**Different outside files with the same basename are counted as one repeated read**

`repeatedReads` groups a session's reads by `repoRelative(path, repoPath)`:

```ts
for (const { path, range, tokens } of read.reads) {
  const shown = repoRelative(path, repoPath);
  const key = `${shown}\u0000${range}`;
```

Since 3d9c6c1, `repoRelative` cuts every path outside the repo (absolute, `~/…`, or `../…`) to its basename. Say one session reads `~/.claude/skills/a/SKILL.md`, `~/.claude/skills/b/SKILL.md` and `~/.claude/skills/c/SKILL.md` with no offset or limit. All three land on the key `SKILL.md\0:`. The group reaches `REPEATED_READS`, a "files read repeatedly" finding is raised, and the second and third files' tokens count as `rereadTokens`, even though no file was read twice. Three sibling repos' `package.json` hit the same case. Inside the repo, `/repo/src/a.ts` and `/repo/.worktrees/w1/src/a.ts` also merge as `src/a.ts`.

Showing the basename is right (the ADR 0150 privacy contract), but the grouping key should be the real path. The cross-session `byPath` merge by display path can stay as it is.

